+## Clarifications
+
+### Session 2026-11-16
+
+- Q: Must the web-page export escape exactly the characters FR-014 names and leave everything else literal, or is any well-formed escaping acceptable? → A: Exactly four substitutions and no others — `&`, `<`, `>` in address, title and labels, plus `"` in the `href` value only; every other character, including `'`, is emitted literally
+- Q: Should a CSV header line of `"id","url","title","tags"` — valid CSV parsing to the same four names — be accepted or rejected? → A: Accepted; the header is compared after CSV parsing, so any valid CSV encoding of the four names in that order is fine, while wrong names, order, count or a missing header still fail with status 2
+- Q: Should an import file that begins with a UTF-8 byte-order mark be read normally or rejected? → A: Read normally; a single leading byte-order mark is discarded before parsing, for both file shapes
+- Q: Should a completely blank line in a table file be ignored or treated as a row with the wrong field count? → A: Treated as a wrong field count and so fails with status 2; the single trailing newline ending the last row is not a blank record and remains valid
+- Q: When a successful import adds nothing against a store path that does not yet exist, is the empty store created or left untouched? → A: Created, as every other command does; only a failed import leaves no store file behind
+
